# Ruby / CocoaPods
/ios/Pods/
/vendor/bundle/
# Regenerated by `pod install` on every run (including in
# .github/workflows/rn-ios-compile.yml) — tracking them only produces churn.
# `Podfile.lock` is deliberately NOT ignored, but be precise about what it
# buys: it RECORDS a known-good pod resolution, it does not PIN the CI one.
# `pod install` re-resolves and may rewrite it, and `--deployment` cannot
# enforce it here — RN 0.73's `React-*` pods come from `node_modules` by path
# and `React-Codegen`'s podspec is generated at install time, so the lock's
# SPEC CHECKSUMS are machine-dependent (measured: identical locally, ~30
# differing React-* digests on macos-15). The reproducible guarantee is the
# `Assert the resolved React matches the pinned React Native` step in
# .github/workflows/rn-ios-compile.yml, which ties React-Core back to the
# react-native version `package-lock.json` pins.
/ios/SceneViewRNDemo.xcworkspace/
/ios/SceneViewRNDemo/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy

# Temporary files created by Metro to check the health of the file watcher
.metro-health-check*

# testing
/coverage
